meta {
  name: tag: uptimekuma (2.4.0)
  type: http
  seq: 12
}

post {
  url: {{base_url}}/pods/templates/uptimekuma/tags
  body: json
  auth: none
}

headers {
  Content-Type: application/json
  X-Tapis-Token: {{X-Tapis-Token}}
}

body:json {
  {
    "kind": "pod",
    "pod_definition": {
      "image": "louislam/uptime-kuma:2.4.0",
      "description": "Single-pod Uptime Kuma with embedded SQLite. No secrets required - the app manages its own login via a first-visit setup wizard. Tapis auth fronts the pod; Kuma's own login is a second layer.",
      "time_to_stop_default": -1,
      "networking": {
        "default": {
          "protocol": "http",
          "port": 3001,
          "tapis_auth": true,
          "tapis_auth_allowed_users": ["*"],
          "tapis_auth_return_path": "/"
        }
      },
      "healthchecks": {
        "readiness": {
          "http_get_path": "/",
          "http_get_port": 3001,
          "initial_delay_seconds": 10,
          "period_seconds": 10
        },
        "liveness": {
          "http_get_path": "/",
          "http_get_port": 3001,
          "initial_delay_seconds": 60,
          "period_seconds": 15
        },
        "networking_requires_ready": true
      }
    },
    "tag": "2.4.0",
    "commit_message": "2.4.0 - health probes, descriptions. Data is ephemeral; see 2.4.0-mariadb stack tag for persistence.",
    "description": "Uptime Kuma 2.4.0 - self-hosted uptime/status monitoring. First visit runs a setup wizard to create the admin account. All state (monitors, users, history) lives in SQLite at /app/data, which is wiped on pod restart - use the 2.4.0-mariadb stack tag if you need durability."
  }
}

docs {
  ## Uptime Kuma 2.4.0 — single pod
  
  Self-hosted uptime/status monitoring. Bumps the old `2.1.1` tag and adds:
  
  - **Health probes** — readiness gates the Tapis URL behind the "service starting" splash
    (`networking_requires_ready: true`); liveness restarts a wedged node process. Kuma returns
    a 3xx redirect on `/` which k8s httpGet probes treat as success.
  - **No secret_map** — there is genuinely nothing to parameterize: Kuma creates its admin
    account through the first-visit setup wizard and stores everything itself.
  
  ### Persistence caveat
  All state is SQLite under `/app/data` on the container filesystem — a restart resets
  monitors, users, and history. For durability use the `2.4.0-mariadb` **stack** tag
  (Stacks → "Create stack template tag (uptimekuma mariadb)"), which moves state into a
  MariaDB member (Kuma 2.x native external-DB support via `UPTIME_KUMA_DB_*` env vars).
}
